### NWS forecast icons
Weather condition icons are derived from the National Weather Service public
forecast icon API (`api.weather.gov/icons`, land day/night set) and related
legacy MapClick codes. Icons are **bundled** under `assets/nws_icons/` for
offline display and to avoid weather.gov CDN blocks on stock Android clients.

Coverage includes clear/sunny, clouds, rain, showers, snow, sleet, freezing
rain, thunder, fog, haze, smoke, dust, wind, hot/cold, blizzard, hurricane,
tropical storm, and tornado (day and night variants where published).

### NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center (SWPC)
Planetary Kp index and geomagnetic scale products from services.swpc.noaa.gov.

### USGS
Earthquake catalog via the USGS Earthquake Hazards Program FDSN event API
(https://earthquake.usgs.gov/). Stream and lake stage (parameter 00065) via
USGS Water Services / NWIS for inland water-level context.

### NOAA National Hurricane Center (NHC)
Active tropical cyclone list and related public products
(e.g. https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/CurrentStorms.json).

### NOAA Storm Prediction Center (SPC)
Preliminary local storm reports (tornado, etc.) from SPC climo report products.

### Open-Meteo
Optional hourly extras (air quality / US AQI, UV index, surface pressure, and
visibility fallback) via https://open-meteo.com/ (open data; free non-commercial
API terms apply). See https://open-meteo.com/en/licence

Inspiration
-----------

User experience was inspired by the commercial Android application
“NOAA Weather & Tides” by Pandamonium Software
(https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pandamonium.noaaweather).

Point Forecast is an independent clean-room implementation. It does not
include that product’s source code, proprietary assets, or branding.
